# mm.rtc.pcf85063

The NXP PCF85063 real-time clock, over portable mm.mcu I2C. It contains no
vendor header and no board pin number: a board's provider supplies the wiring
and this module drives the protocol.

Registers are eight-bit and the calendar is packed binary-coded decimal, so
every field crosses this boundary twice: once as BCD on the wire and once as an
ordinary number in mm.rtc's DateTime. The part stores two year digits, so this
driver fixes the century at 2000 and refuses a year outside it rather than
wrapping one silently.

Modelled on Waveshare's reference driver for the RP2350-Touch-LCD-2.8. Two
things differ. The reference reports oscillator stop by printing; here it is the
trusted flag mm.rtc requires, read from the same seconds byte the time came from
rather than from a second transaction. The reference converts through struct tm
and mktime; mm.rtc has its own calendar so that a freestanding lane needs no
<ctime>, and the month and year offsets tm imposes are gone with it.
